  "new_issue_decision": "CREATED",
  "observable_outcome": "Cycle #23 said VENUE_AND_SITE was admitted for all one hundred eighty-two oriented Week 1 rows even though not one row carried an authoritative venue. The successor splits that single field into three, and the split is what makes the difference visible: SITE_ORIENTATION is admitted one hundred eighty-two times because the schedule genuinely orients every contest, VENUE_IDENTITY is SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ABSENT one hundred eighty-two times, and VENUE_COORDINATES is candidate-only one hundred eighty-two times, so weather can never be promoted into model input from an inference. The successor also stops describing a missing 2026 prior as a prior nobody could know: one hundred seventy-four rows are STALE_ALLOWED_HISTORY_AVAILABLE because through-2023 evidence exists but has not been frozen into a current surface, and eight rows are UNRESOLVED_ENTITY. PARTIAL_MODEL_INPUT is retained as a diagnostic but maps to ABSTAIN_MISSING_REQUIRED_FEATURES at forecast time, so no candidate can emit a probability from partial input. The ambiguous pair-level admitted_domain_count is retired: for Texas A&M against Missouri State the reported four is proven to be four admitted team-domain cells across two oriented rows, not four distinct domains, of which there are two. No predecessor gate, payload or identity is rewritten.",
